        <dcterms:identifier>SENSITIVE</dcterms:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateAccepted rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2020-03-11</dcterms:dateAccepted>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2020-02-25</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/access-right/NON_PUBLIC" />
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">statut d&#39;accès aux ressources contenant des informations sensibles non classifiées (SNC), c&#39;est-à-dire des informations dont la divulgation non autorisée pourrait porter préjudice à la Commission ou à d&#39;autres parties concernées, telles que des entreprises, des sociétés, la propriété intellectuelle ou des données à caractère personnel, mais qui ne constituent pas des informations classifiées de l&#39;UE</skos:definition>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">access status for resources containing sensitive non-classified (SNC) information, that is, information whose unauthorised disclosure could cause damage to the Commission or other interested parties, such as businesses, companies, intellectual property, or personal data, but which is not EU classified information</skos:definition>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Sensitive non-classified resources may contain personal data, but this is not a defining criterion. Information on the presence of personal data should be provided separately. This category covers information that requires protection even though it is not subject to formal EU security classification.</skos:scopeNote>
        <ns9:authority-code>SENSITIVE</ns9:authority-code>
        <ns9:deprecated>false</ns9:deprecated>
        <ns9:op-code>SENSITIVE</ns9:op-code>
        <ns9:start.use>2020-03-18</ns9:start.use>
